f("DFM-8","both","minor",["U7","U1","U9","U10","U13","U14","J3","U8","U15","U16"],[],"Both boards are ordered HASL but carry 0.4-0.5 mm pitch QFN/DFN (CH224Q 0.224 mm pads, ES7243E, ES8388 0.45, LAN8720A, ES9018K2M) and a 0.5 mm FFC. Uneven HASL on small pads risks floating parts and opens.","Job files: Finish HASL. Footprint pad widths 0.224-0.23 mm. JLC capability page warns of HASL short risk on fine features and requires ENIG for 0.2-0.25 pads.","Order ENIG on both boards (a few tens of $ per 5-board order, unverified).","Pad 0.224 mm on 0.40 pitch with HASL")
f("DFM-9","both","minor",["U8","U7","U1","U10","U9"],["GND"],"EP paste is 100 % (no paste ratio anywhere) except Lite U8, whose 4 windows sit right on its 16 open 0.3 mm vias. ES8388, CH224A, ES9018K2M and LAN8720A EPs have open vias under 100 % paste. Core ESP32 pad 2 has an open via in the pad.","Board pad dump: 0 solder_paste_margin entries; U8 windows 7.84/14.1 mm2 = 55 % but each window holds 4 vias; via counts in EP: Lite U7 1, U1 3, U8 16; core U10 9, U9 1.","Window EP paste to 50-70 % between the vias (solder_paste_margin_ratio -0.2..-0.3 or explicit windows). Move U8's windows off the via rows. Move core U7 pad-2 via about 0.5 mm off the pad. Option: JLC filled/capped via-in-pad.","EP float risk at 100 % paste")
